course: dictionary
lesson: 4424
title: One word, different meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning the writer wants. «Communities help each other: a family that receives a £40 hamper one year may give one the next.» Here a hamper is a gift basket full of food, because people give and receive it.
explain: The same word can also be a verb, an action word. «The rescue was hampered by bad weather.» Bad weather cannot be a basket, so hampered must be a different meaning: the weather made the rescue harder or slower. Ask yourself, what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence.
explain: In the UK, Ireland and Australia, a hamper at Christmas is a gift full of treats. In America, a hamper is where dirty clothes go. Both are baskets, but the place you find them tells you which one is meant.
fact: A hamper is a large basket with a lid.
fact: A picnic hamper carries food for a day out.
fact: A Christmas hamper is a gift basket full of food and treats.
fact: In the US, a laundry hamper is a basket for dirty clothes.
fact: To hamper means to get in the way of something and make it slower or harder.
exercise: «Communities help each other: a family that receives a £40 hamper one year may give one the next.» What is a hamper here? | A bag for dirty clothes | A kind of tent | A small box for keys | *A gift basket full of food
exercise: «The rescue was hampered by bad weather.» What does hampered mean? | Made warmer | Packed into a picnic | *Made harder or slower | Made faster and easier
exercise: Which phrase means a basket for dirty clothes in America? | Gift hamper | Christmas hamper | *Laundry hamper | Picnic hamper
test: Mum packed the sandwiches and crisps into a picnic hamper. What is the hamper? | A kind of shoe | Basket for dirty laundry | *Large basket with a lid for food
test: «Heavy snow will hamper the trains.» What does hamper mean here? | *Get in the way and slow down | Help | Cover with paint
exam: The word hamper can be a noun or a verb. Which sentence uses hamper as a verb? | We ate our lunch from the picnic hamper | Grandma sent us a Christmas hamper | *Strong winds may hamper our walk to school | Dad put the wet towels in the laundry hamper
